PUBLIC RESPONSE: {C. None of the above is correct.

The data show that the ADC is substantially more potent than anti-TNF at suppressing inflammation (ear-swelling and paw-swelling assays) while producing markedly less bone loss at the same 10 mg/kg dose. GRM also suppresses swelling and causes little bone loss, but was tested at only 3 mg/kg, so direct side-effect comparisons at equal doses are impossible. No listed statement is fully consistent with these results: statements claiming “same risk of osteoporosis,” incorrect potency rankings, or unsupported dose-equivalence conclusions are contradicted by the experiments.}

(The dosage chosen for GRM in Exp. 3 prevents any firm statement that GRM would remain safer at 10 mg/kg; the claim that GRM “cannot fight inflammation” is simply false.)

